      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60329075ba9b3b1a4eb315c4|full_name}: The kicker here is that Children under the age of 13 are not supposed to have their own accounts on VRchat.  That actually places a whole lot of burden on VRchat to comply with COPPA.  Personally I think VRchat should stop making Steam and Occulus accounts and require registration from the get go so that Parents who are activating the game for their children are given a chance to see what exactly their children are doing. I have a feeling that the extra step would dissuade parents from letting their kids on VRchat.  As it is right now you just have to download the app in either store and an account is just created for you.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
