  "details": "Looking at other services dealing with an influx of children, They've come up with solutions without impacting player numbers. They've created Junior accounts where they are filtered to officially curated content\nVRC can enable the same features without impact to the rest of the app.\n\n.\n.\n.\n\nThis Benefits for everyone: \n-This will keep kids safe online, in curated content\naway from malicious individuals\n-VRC+ is not affected, it keeps  working the way it is but it allows for new \"content packs\" to be introduced\n-Avatars could follow Minecraft's example and be distributed using cosmetic packs for avatars\n-VRC+ could be used to enable access to these packs without purchase, for the duration of the subscription\n-- This continuously allows devs to keep a subscription flow without interruption or legal risk\n-Worlds would be filtered to prevent non-JUNIOR or associated accounts from joining worlds\n\n.\n.\n.\n\nThe Moderation flow would be easier to manage:\n-Junior Accounts can't upload custom content, allowing curated content to be the backbone of the service\n-Juniors would have their own exclusive moderators not to muddy the waters of acceptable behavior\n-No fullbody for Juniors (no humping, no strip clubs)\n-Anyone recognized as a Junior can have their account set as Junior status without having to ban them. \n-None of this will affect Traditional VRChat, only making it to easier for users to report Juniors back to their curated content\n\n.\n.\n.\n\nCons:\n-Some of the issues would be \"what if they're using a voice changers?\" \n--Concealing your voice is a punishable offense to Junior accounts, and just simply making sure anyone trying to sneak into Jr world would be stopped immediately, such as pretending to be mute\n---People trying to sneak into Junior worlds can be banned and reported, making it easier to report for intent for legal reasons.\n\n.\n.\n.\n\nIn the long run, this keeps younger users safe without pushing out potential income",
